      "narrative": "The copper lamps flicker as you approach Mara Venn's table. She looks up from a half-empty tankard, charcoal coat shifting as she sets down her drink.\n\n\"Ash Gate?\" She tilts her head, studying you with those sharp eyes. \"Seems you've heard the wrong stories.\"\n\nShe leans forward, and you lean in too\u2014eager, maybe a little too eager. Your boot catches the leg of a nearby chair. It scrapes across the floorboards with a harsh *screech*. A few heads turn. Toran Vex flinches at the sound, ink-stained fingers tightening around his cup.\n\nMara's eyes narrow. Not at the noise\u2014at *you*. She saw you flinch, saw you fumble. Her expression cools by a degree.\n\n\"Easy now,\" she says, voice dropping. \"You're wound tight as a bowstring. What's your angle here? Looking for work, or looking to make trouble?\"\n\nShe hasn't answered your question. She's asking one of her own now, and the silence stretches as she waits\u2014her gaze pinned on you, reading every twitch.\n\n*What do you say to her?*..."
    },
