      "narrative": "Mara's eyes flicker\u2014a brief, telling pause. She was ready for bravado or bluster, not a precise question about the gate's mechanics.\n\nShe settles back, hooking a thumb toward the bar. \"You want the lockwright. Toran Vex\u2014clerk with the ink-stained cuffs, over by the counter. He's the one who kept that lock turning for years. Sworn to the Kestrel Guild and all.\"\n\nShe tilts her head, watching your reaction. \"The Guild doesn't take just anyone. Means he knew that gate better than anyone breathing. Ask *him*\u2014if he'll talk. He's been jumpy as a cat in a kennel since the gate was sealed.\"\n\nShe picks up her tankard, taking a long drink, her attention drifting to the bar\u2014a clear signal the conversation's turn has passed.\n\nToran Vex is hunched at the counter, his back to the room, shoulders tight. A half-finished ledger lies open beside his elbow, untouched for some time.\n\n*What do you do?*..."
    },
