      "narrative": "You hold her gaze and press. \"Who sold passage, Mara? By name.\"\n\nShe sets the tankard down slowly, the dull thud against wood carrying weight. Her eyes hold yours for a long moment\u2014then she gives a single, tight nod, convinced you're serious.\n\n\"Old Bram,\" she says. Quiet. Flat. \"He was the ferryman. Ran a skiff through the mist on the other side, knew the channels, knew the tolls. Took coin, took favors, never asked questions.\"\n\nShe reaches for her drink again, but doesn't lift it\u2014just fingers the rim. \"He's dead now. Found face-down at the gate three mornings ago. That's when they sealed it.\"\n\nShe lets that land, watching you. \"So if you're chasing the man who sold the passage, you're chasing a corpse. And corpses don't talk.\"\n\n*The air settles heavy. The question hangs: what do you do with a dead lead?*..."
    },
